From ea2f558fbc7ad14cbc348f9a2c3b7b00b72a4c9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Huy Nguyen <tuonghuy@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 22:59:36 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] Reject writes to a split parent during an in-progress
 in-place split

Closes a silent data-loss window in in-place shard split. Ordinary indexing
routes to the still-STARTED parent while the children each clone the parent's
then-latest published manifest once, at their own recovery time. Any document
the parent acknowledged after a child had cloned but before the split committed
landed only in a later parent manifest generation that no child references, and
became permanently unreachable once the parent's routing was retired at commit.

Fix: reject new primary writes on a shard while it is the parent of an
in-progress split (IndexShard.ensureWriteAllowed calls a new
ensureNotInProgressSplitParent), throwing IllegalIndexShardStateException. That
is a shard-not-available (retriable) exception, so the write fails fast and
succeeds once it re-routes to a committed child, which is the same behaviour a
relocating or closing shard already has. Simpler and more obviously correct than
synchronous dual-write across two engines mid-recovery; the split design already
accepts a recovery-time cost, so a short write-rejection window is acceptable.

Having chosen reject-writes over dual-write, this also removes the scaffolding
left in place for the dual-write path that the feature never wired up. All of it
is dead: across server, plugins, modules and libs, ShardRoutingState.SPLITTING
appears only inside ShardRouting and its own enum declaration, so nothing ever
puts a shard into that state and byte 5 is never written to the wire; and
ShardRouting.splitting/isSplitTarget/getParentShardId/getRecoveringChildShards
and OperationRouting.shardWithRecoveringChild have no callers outside the two
files declaring them. Also drops the includeInProgressChildren branch and
parameter threaded through generateShardId/getShardIdOfHash, which only that
scaffolding ever passed true for.

Test: IndexShardTests.testRejectsPrimaryWriteWhileInPlaceSplitInProgress indexes
a doc, marks the shard an in-progress split parent, and asserts index and delete
are both rejected with a retriable shard-not-available exception. Verified by
removing the guard, which fails the test.

Signed-off-by: Huy Nguyen <tuonghuy@gmail.com>
